 "changed_since_previous": "Dropped changes to `AllocateFileRange` for Windows and the zero-fill fallback, narrowing the PR strictly to checking for an existing genesis block in `LoadGenesisBlock()` in `src/validation.cpp`.",
 "card": "Avoids silent destruction of block data on platforms without native `posix_fallocate` (*BSD, OmniOS) when the block index is missing or corrupted. `LoadGenesisBlock()` now checks for an existing genesis block in `blk00000.dat` and updates block file metadata rather than unconditionally rewriting it from position zero. This prevents the zero-filling file allocation fallback from overwriting subsequent blocks in the file, fixing issue #33128.",
